# =============================================================================
# PF (Packet Filter) Access Control Rules for Backend Services (Mac 3)
# =============================================================================
# Machine: Mac 3 (Saksham - 10.200.251.76)
# Services:
#   - Backend A: TCP port 3001
#   - Backend B: TCP port 3002
#
# Security Policy (Requirement C):
#   - Only authorized edge nodes (Mac 1 standby edge and Mac 2 primary edge)
#     can access backend ports.
#   - Local loopback (127.0.0.1) is allowed for health checks and local monitoring.
#   - All other inbound connections to ports 3001 and 3002 MUST be denied.
# =============================================================================

# Define Authorized Edge Hosts
table <authorized_edges> { 127.0.0.1, 10.200.251.106, 10.200.251.227 }

# Allow local loopback traffic
pass in quick on lo0 proto tcp to any port { 3001, 3002 }

# Allow traffic strictly from authorized edge nodes
pass in quick proto tcp from <authorized_edges> to any port { 3001, 3002 }

# Block and drop all other traffic to backend ports
block drop in quick proto tcp to any port { 3001, 3002 }
